Fix rendering freeze after first frame introduced by
webkit-sticky-scroll-composite-sync-env.patch (build 420).

The compositor-thread applyLayerPositionsWhileLocked() call writes layer
positions via setPositionForScrolling(), whose notifyCompositionRequired()
reached LayerTreeHost::notifyCompositionRequired() from the COMPOSITOR
thread and set the main-thread-owned m_compositionRequired flag. That left
a stale "composition required" signal with no composite scheduled:
ScrollingTreeCoordinated::didCompleteRenderingUpdate() then saw
isCompositionRequiredOrOngoing() and waited forever for a
didCompletePlatformRenderingUpdate() (which only fires after a real
composite via didRenderFrame), so the rendering-update cycle never
returned to Idle and the webview froze after the first frame.

Two fixes:
1. LayerTreeHost::notifyCompositionRequired(): ignore calls made on the
   compositing run loop — such changes are consumed immediately by the
   in-progress flush and must not request another composite.
2. ThreadedCompositor::flushCompositingState(): only take the tree-locked
   re-apply path for composites whose reasons consume Position/BoundsOrigin
   (RenderingUpdate/AsyncScrolling); VideoFrame/Animation-only composites
   leave position changes pending anyway.

diff -u -r a/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/LayerTreeHost.cpp c/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/LayerTreeHost.cpp
--- a/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/LayerTreeHost.cpp	2026-07-02 10:42:37.956094912 +0000
+++ b/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/LayerTreeHost.cpp	2026-07-02 12:03:06.709203783 +0000
@@ -411,6 +411,15 @@
         m_compositionRequiredInScrollingThread = true;
         return;
     }
+    // Layer position changes applied by the compositor thread itself right
+    // before its layer flush (WEBKIT_COMPOSITE_SCROLL_SYNC) are consumed by
+    // that very flush. Setting m_compositionRequired for them would leave a
+    // stale "composition required" signal with no composite scheduled, making
+    // ScrollingTreeCoordinated::didCompleteRenderingUpdate wait forever for a
+    // didCompletePlatformRenderingUpdate() that never comes — rendering
+    // freezes after the first frame.
+    if (m_compositor && m_compositor->runLoop() == &RunLoop::currentSingleton())
+        return;
 #endif
     m_compositionRequired = true;
 }
diff -u -r a/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/ThreadedCompositor.cpp c/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/ThreadedCompositor.cpp
--- a/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/ThreadedCompositor.cpp	2026-07-02 10:42:37.956094912 +0000
+++ b/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/ThreadedCompositor.cpp	2026-07-02 12:03:06.710203790 +0000
@@ -288,7 +288,10 @@
